WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.368
-Welcome back.
Our next guest

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.337
is a talented actress
you know from movies such as

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.773
"The King of Staten Island"
and "Assassination Nation."

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:10.075
She currently stars as Lexi in
the hit HBO series "Euphoria."

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:12.879
The season finale airs
this Sunday at 900 p.m.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.914
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.350
-I need you to pull it way back.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.288
You're too broad.
It's not funny.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.623
-[ Sniffles ]

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.791
-Oh, are you crying?

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:26.960
It's a directorial note.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.596
You just take it and move on,
okay?

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.899
Hey, I need the light cues
to be 40% faster

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.734
and the stagehands
to be 20% faster.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.302
-Copy that.
-Ew!

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:40.172
God, what the --
Did someone die in this dress?

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:41.707
It smells like [bleep]

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:44.110
Ugh!

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.646
[Bleep]

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.515
I love the theater.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:51.184
-Please welcome to the show
Maude Apatow!

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.186
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.186 --> 00:01:03.196 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:09.736 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:13.305
-Hi, Maude!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:15.174
We are so happy
to have you here.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:16.742
-Oh, my gosh,
I'm so excited to be here.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:18.711
-And you genuinely --

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.713
Look, it's a fantastic
acting performance,

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.815
but you do genuinely
love the theater.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:23.983
-Of course.
-That was a line that must have

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.385
been easy for you to say.
-Yes.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:28.254
No, Sam and I had a lot of
discussions about it beforehand,

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:32.225
and it was loosely based on me
as a theater child.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:35.427
-And you were very early
into the theater, yes?

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:38.564
-Yes. So, I started
when I was really young.

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:41.133
I remember I always, like,
really went for it, too.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:44.303
So, like, my first --
I did, like, a gold-rush day,

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.239
and I wanted to look
like a miner.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.708
So I, like,
ripped out my tooth to, like,

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.110
look more like a --
-Was it a loose tooth?

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.811
-It was not a loose tooth
at all.

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:54.914
-Oh, no!
-It was not ready to go,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.383
and I just ripped it out.
-How old?

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.951
What age are we talking about?

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.453
-I think I was 9.
-This is way --

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:03.389
-But I was dedicated.
-They say people should not

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.791
go method
until they're like 12 or 13.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:07.193
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.362
-What did -- Your parents,
I should note, have both been

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.531
guests on this show,
Judd and Leslie.

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.933
And what did they --
how did they react

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:17.136
when you took out a tooth for
the purposes of a school play?

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:20.106
-I think my dad was like,
"What is wrong with her?

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.408
Oh, no.
We've raised a monster."

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:26.011
But, no, that's -- and then it
just got worse as I got older.

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:28.481
Like, I --
Yeah, I just became a tyrant.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.849
-Yeah.
So, and would you --

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.951
Do you think that those who were
in your early school plays

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.586
would reflect back
and say that was --

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.887
-Of course.
-Yeah, okay, gotcha.

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.556
-Yeah, yeah.
No, I got a couple texts

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.658
when the show aired, like,
"Triggered."

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.859
Like --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:43.062
I was like, "Oh, no!"
But I remember, like,

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.198
senior year of high school,
I was doing a play,

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:47.967
and, like, the pinnacle moment
of the play, this kid, like,

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.535
is supposed to slap me
in the face.

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.170
-What was the play?
-It was "Cabaret."

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.805
-Okay, gotcha.
I was like, these --

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.540
I don't know if you should do
"slap in the face" plays

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.576
in high school.
-Probably not.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:03:00.947
But he, like, did this, like,
goofy slap, and I was so mad.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.149
I was like, "God,
this is ruining the moment.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.984
Like, come on.
Like, slap me for real."

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.319
And he's like, "No, no, no,
I don't want to do that."

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.053
I'm like,
"You're embarrassing me.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.322
Like, you're
embarrassing yourself.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.890
Just do it."
And he, like,

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.560
slapped me really hard
in the show.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.227
So, like, I think
I made him really mad.

00:03:15.227 --> 00:03:16.329
-Oh, my God.
-So when we were actually

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.597
doing it, yeah.
-He was probably like,

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.365
"I don't want to slap
another tooth out."

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:22.034
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.936
-But it caught me off guard
how hard he slapped me.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:25.104
He really went for it
during the show.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.372
-Yeah, oh, my gosh.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.639
-And I was
really happy about it.

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:29.308
-A real commitment.
This is --

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:30.509
You do seem
really happy in this.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:31.944
So, this is a production of --

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.780
Where in high school
are you for "Grease"?

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.414
-Oh, no, that's not high school.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:36.615
All right, good.
-That's --

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.518
I think I was 9 or 10.
-9 or 10.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.486
This is a production
of "Grease."

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:44.356
And I would just like
to point out, only person

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:46.259
in this photo who seems to know
where the camera is.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.127
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.729
-It's an aggressive jazz hand.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.466
-It is a very aggressive
jazz hand.

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.835
Well, I'm sure your entire cast
of "Grease"

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:58.871
is very proud of you right now.
-I hope so.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.840
-You and I
have something in common.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.675
We both went to
Northwestern University.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.943
-Yeah.
-Your career took off

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:06.112
a little bit faster than mine,
and you were there

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:09.848
for a couple of years,
and then, you basically --

00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:12.185
you know, you didn't
need the rest of it.

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.986
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:16.322
No, I, uh -- I had a great time
at Northwestern.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.791
I left to shoot "Euphoria,"
but --

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.593
-That's a good reason.
That's a good reason to go.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.961
-Yeah.
-If I would've left,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.762
it would've been, like,
to go back to my job

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:25.164
as a sub delivery guy.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.398
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:28.534
Did you -- But you want
to clear something up

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.402
about your time at Northwestern.

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:33.172
-Okay.
So, my freshman year,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:36.642
in the dorm bathroom,
there was a bath,

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.144
and no one would ever
go in the bath.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.545
-No, of course.
You would never.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.913
-No, no, no.
Like, it was foul.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.082
-It's bad enough
you have to go in the shower.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.318
-Yeah, yeah.
The bath was, like,

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:49.054
covered in, like,
fungus and spores.

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:51.757
And, like, I remember it was
like orange mold sort of.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.660
-Yeah.
-And I was brushing my teeth

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.862
one night, and a girl came up
to me, and she's like,

00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:58.931
"Heard you've been
going in the bath."

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:01.634
And I was like, "What? No."

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.802
I was like,
"That's so weird. What?"

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:05.805
'Cause I hadn't.
And then I went up

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.506
to my friend Sydney, I was like,
"It's so funny.

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:09.809
Like, this girl came up to me,
she said that she heard

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.477
I was going in the bath,"
and she's like,

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.345
"Yeah, I heard that, too."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:15.281
So, I guess there's a rumor
that I was bathing in, like,

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:18.384
this really disgusting bath,
and I wasn't, so...

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.685
[ Laughter ]
-That's good.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.154
So we want to say right now,
on national television...

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:23.222
-It didn't happen.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.724
-...the bath thing
never happened.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.759
-Yes.
-And, also, I mean,

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.761
those bathrooms -- like, I mean,
there are a bunch of people.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.063
It would be impossible to take
a bath in a college bathroom

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:32.564
without people
walking in on you.

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:34.834
-Right? Or I was doing it
at like 3:00 a.m.?

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:38.037
-Yeah. I will say, it would be
a very boss move

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:41.674
to just take a bath
in a dorm bathroom

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:44.010
and just have people walk in
and be like, "Hey!"

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.746
-Fully sprawled out.
-Yeah.

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:49.548
Like, "Hey, do you need --
do you need the bath?

00:05:49.548 --> 00:05:51.684
I can get out."
It's like, "No, we're good."

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.219
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:55.821
-That's horrible.
What dorm were you in?

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:58.024
-I was in Willard my first year.
Which dorm were you in?

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.491
-I was in Elder.
-Elder, yeah.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:00.927
Oh, you were the girl
who took the bath!

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:03.195
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.195 --> 00:06:05.364
-Aah!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:07.100
-I heard that --
This was in the alumni magazine.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.402
Now I'm putting it all together.

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:11.103
I have a lot more questions
about "Euphoria."

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:13.373
We'll be right back
with more from Maude Apatow.

